module

public import Grothendieck.Folder55

/-!
# Folder 55, page 13: Lemme B does not hold as stated

Page 13 of folder 55 states, without proof, a « Lemme B »: if a ringed space `X` is
quasi-compact (i), has a coherent structure sheaf (ii) and noetherian local rings (iv), and
satisfies the identity principle (v) — for every coherent Ideal `𝒥`, with
`Y = (Supp 𝒪_X/𝒥, 𝒪_X/𝒥)`, every `y ∈ Y` at which `𝒪_{Y,y}` is a domain has an open
neighbourhood `U` in `Y` on which a section of `𝒪_Y` vanishing near `y` vanishes — then every
increasing sequence of coherent subsheaves of a coherent sheaf is stationary.
`Grothendieck/Folder55.lean` proves the lemma with (v) replaced by a uniformity hypothesis
(`Folder55.stationary_of_germs`). This file shows that (v) does not give that uniformity, and
that the lemma, read for an arbitrary ringed space, is false.

## Main results

The ring data are kept abstract: rings `k`, `D`, `K` with ring maps `κ : k → D` (constants),
`ε : D → k` (constant term) and `ι : D → K` (inclusion), with `ε ∘ κ = id` and `ι` injective;
for `k[[t]] ⊂ k((t))` these hold.

* `instCompactSpacePt`: (i), `X` is quasi-compact.
* `O`: the structure sheaf, as a subsheaf (in the sense of `Folder55.Subsheaf`) of the sheaf of
  all functions with values `k`, `D × D`, `K` at the points; it is closed under `1`, `+`, `*`
  (`O_one_mem`, `O_add_mem`, `O_mul_mem`).
* `G`: the Ideals `𝒢_j`, contained in `O` and stable under `+` and multiplication by `O`
  (`G_le_O`, `G_add_mem`, `G_mul_mem`), increasing (`G_mono`), not stationary
  (`G_not_stationary`).
* `rigid`, `identity_principle`: (v) for `𝒪` at `∞` on each `B_M`.
* `G_germs_inf`, `G_germs_stabilize`: the germs of the `𝒢_j` stabilise at every point.
* `G_not_uniform`: the uniformity hypothesis of `Folder55.stationary_of_germs` fails;
  `identity_principle_not_enough` gathers it.

**Proved in the companion files.** `Grothendieck/Folder55Coherent.lean` and
`Grothendieck/Folder55Ideals.lean` prove the coherence (Stacks 01BV,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`) of `𝒪` and of the `𝒢_j` and the noetherianity of the stalks,
and gather the counterexample over `k⟦X⟧ ⊂ k⸨X⸩` (`lemmeB_counterexample`).

## Implementation notes

### The counterexample

Fix a field `k`, `D = k[[t]]`, `K = k((t))`. The space `X` has a point `∞` and, for each
`n : ℕ`, four points `cₙ, eₙ, oₙ, dₙ`. Its open sets are the sets `U` with
`cₙ ∈ U → oₙ, dₙ ∈ U`, `eₙ ∈ U → oₙ ∈ U`, and, if `∞ ∈ U`, `U ⊇ B_N` for some `N`, where
`B_N = {∞} ∪ {all dₙ} ∪ {cₙ, eₙ, oₙ : n ≥ N}`. Every point but `∞` has a smallest open
neighbourhood; the `B_N` are a fundamental system of neighbourhoods of `∞`. The structure sheaf
has stalks `k` at `∞` and at `eₙ`, the node `R = D ×_k D ≅ k[[x, y]]/(xy)` at `cₙ`, and `K` at
`oₙ` and `dₙ`; `R` maps to `K` at `oₙ` by its first branch and at `dₙ` by its second, `k` maps
to `K` at `oₙ` by the constants, and near `∞` a section is a constant of `k`.

* (i) A cover has a member containing some `B_N`, and only finitely many points lie outside it.
* (iv) The stalks `k`, `R`, `K` are noetherian local rings.
* (ii) At a point with a smallest neighbourhood, coherence of `𝒪` comes from noetherian stalks
  and flat specialisation maps (`R → K` are the localisations at the two minimal primes, and
  `k → K` is flat). Near `∞`, sections over `B_N` are constants of `k`, so the kernel of a
  finite family of them is spanned by constant sections.
* (v) At a point with a smallest open neighbourhood `V`, sections over `V` are the stalk.
  At `∞` the stalk `k` is a field: if `∞ ∈ Supp 𝒪/𝒥` then `𝒥_∞ = 0`, so `𝒥`, of finite type,
  vanishes on some `B_M`, where `𝒪_Y = 𝒪`; and on every `B_M`, a section of `𝒪` vanishing near
  `∞` vanishes (`identity_principle`): it vanishes at every `dₙ`, and on each piece
  `{cₙ, eₙ, oₙ, dₙ}` a section is determined by its value at `dₙ` (`rigid`), because the value
  at `eₙ` lies in `k` and must agree with the first branch at `cₙ`, whose constant term is that
  of the second branch.
* `𝒢_j`, the Ideal of sections vanishing at `∞`, at every `dₙ` and on the pieces `n ≥ j`, is
  coherent: it is `0` on `B_j`, it is generated by `(t, 0)` at `cₙ` and by `1` at `eₙ`. The
  sequence `𝒢_j` increases and is not stationary (`G_not_stationary`): `𝒢_{j+1}` has the
  section `1` over `{e_j, o_j}`, `𝒢_j` does not.

So Lemme B fails for `F = 𝒪_X`. What breaks is the step from germs to a neighbourhood: all `𝒢_j`
have germ `0` at `∞`, yet no neighbourhood of `∞` sees them stabilise. The identity principle
holds on the fundamental system `B_M`, and still `Γ(B_M, 𝒢_j) = 0` while `𝒢_j ≠ 0` on `B_M`
for `j > M` (`G_sections_basic`): the `𝒢_j` are not generated by their sections over the
privileged neighbourhoods, which is what Frisch's version of the argument (privileged
neighbourhoods on a Stein compact, where theorem A holds) also uses.

`Grothendieck/Folder55Quotients.lean` builds the quotient sheaves `𝒪/𝒥` and their supports, and
proves (v) for every coherent Ideal `𝒥` (`identity_principle_quotient'`). So the counterexample
satisfies (i), (ii), (iv) and (v) as stated (`lemmeB_counterexample_v`).

## Not formalised

`Y = Supp 𝒪/𝒥` is not built as a ringed space in its own right: (v) is stated on `X`, through
the sheaf `𝒪/𝒥`, the direct image of `𝒪_Y` (see `Grothendieck/Folder55Quotients.lean`).

## References

* A. Grothendieck, folder 55, p. 13 (Lemme B)
* Stacks Project, tag 01BV
* Frisch's version of the argument (privileged neighbourhoods on a Stein compact)
-/

@[expose] public section


open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite

namespace Grothendieck.Folder55LemmaB

/-! ### The space -/

/-- The points: `infty`, and for each `n` a node `c n`, a point `e n`, and two generic points
`o n`, `d n`. -/
inductive Pt : Type
  | infty : Pt
  | c : ℕ → Pt
  | e : ℕ → Pt
  | o : ℕ → Pt
  | d : ℕ → Pt

open Pt

/-- `InBasic N y`: `y` lies in the basic neighbourhood `B_N` of `infty`. -/
def InBasic (N : ℕ) : Pt → Prop
  | infty => True
  | c n => N ≤ n
  | e n => N ≤ n
  | o n => N ≤ n
  | d _ => True

/-- The basic neighbourhood `B_N = {infty} ∪ {d n} ∪ {c n, e n, o n : n ≥ N}`. -/
def basic (N : ℕ) : Set Pt := {y | InBasic N y}

theorem inBasic_anti {N M : ℕ} (h : N ≤ M) : ∀ y, InBasic M y → InBasic N y
  | infty, _ => trivial
  | c _, hy => le_trans h hy
  | e _, hy => le_trans h hy
  | o _, hy => le_trans h hy
  | d _, _ => trivial

theorem basic_anti {N M : ℕ} (h : N ≤ M) : basic M ⊆ basic N := fun y hy => inBasic_anti h y hy

/-- The open sets. -/
def IsOpenPt (U : Set Pt) : Prop :=
  (∀ n, c n ∈ U → o n ∈ U ∧ d n ∈ U) ∧ (∀ n, e n ∈ U → o n ∈ U) ∧
    (infty ∈ U → ∃ N, basic N ⊆ U)

instance : TopologicalSpace Pt where
  IsOpen := IsOpenPt
  isOpen_univ := ⟨fun _ _ => ⟨Set.mem_univ _, Set.mem_univ _⟩, fun _ _ => Set.mem_univ _,
    fun _ => ⟨0, Set.subset_univ _⟩⟩
  isOpen_inter U V hU hV := by
    refine ⟨fun n h => ⟨⟨(hU.1 n h.1).1, (hV.1 n h.2).1⟩, ⟨(hU.1 n h.1).2, (hV.1 n h.2).2⟩⟩,
      fun n h => ⟨hU.2.1 n h.1, hV.2.1 n h.2⟩, fun h => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨N₁, h₁⟩ := hU.2.2 h.1
    obtain ⟨N₂, h₂⟩ := hV.2.2 h.2
    exact ⟨max N₁ N₂, fun y hy =>
      ⟨h₁ (basic_anti (le_max_left _ _) hy), h₂ (basic_anti (le_max_right _ _) hy)⟩⟩
  isOpen_sUnion S hS := by
    refine ⟨fun n h => ?_, fun n h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨t, ht, hct⟩ := Set.mem_sUnion.1 h
      exact ⟨Set.mem_sUnion_of_mem ((hS t ht).1 n hct).1 ht,
        Set.mem_sUnion_of_mem ((hS t ht).1 n hct).2 ht⟩
    · obtain ⟨t, ht, het⟩ := Set.mem_sUnion.1 h
      exact Set.mem_sUnion_of_mem ((hS t ht).2.1 n het) ht
    · obtain ⟨t, ht, hit⟩ := Set.mem_sUnion.1 h
      obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := (hS t ht).2.2 hit
      exact ⟨N, hN.trans (Set.subset_sUnion_of_mem ht)⟩

theorem isOpenPt_iff {U : Set Pt} : IsOpen U ↔ IsOpenPt U := Iff.rfl

/-- **(i)**: the space is quasi-compact. -/
instance instCompactSpacePt : CompactSpace Pt := by
  refine ⟨isCompact_iff_finite_subcover.2 fun {ι} U hU hcov => ?_⟩
  classical
  choose f hf using fun y : Pt => Set.mem_iUnion.1 (hcov (Set.mem_univ y))
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := (isOpenPt_iff.1 (hU (f infty))).2.2 (hf infty)
  let t : Finset ι := insert (f infty) ((Finset.range N).image (fun n => f (c n)) ∪
    (Finset.range N).image (fun n => f (e n)) ∪ (Finset.range N).image (fun n => f (o n)))
  refine ⟨t, fun y _ => ?_⟩
  have key : ∀ i ∈ t, y ∈ U i → y ∈ ⋃ i ∈ t, U i := fun i hi hy => by
    simp only [Set.mem_iUnion]
    exact ⟨i, hi, hy⟩
  have h0 : f infty ∈ t := Finset.mem_insert_self _ _
  cases y with
  | infty => exact key _ h0 (hf infty)
  | d n => exact key _ h0 (hN (show d n ∈ basic N from trivial))
  | c n =>
    by_cases hn : N ≤ n
    · exact key _ h0 (hN (show c n ∈ basic N from hn))
    · exact key (f (c n)) (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_union_left _
        (Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_range.2 (by omega))))))
        (hf (c n))
  | e n =>
    by_cases hn : N ≤ n
    · exact key _ h0 (hN (show e n ∈ basic N from hn))
    · exact key (f (e n)) (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_union_left _
        (Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_range.2 (by omega))))))
        (hf (e n))
  | o n =>
    by_cases hn : N ≤ n
    · exact key _ h0 (hN (show o n ∈ basic N from hn))
    · exact key (f (o n)) (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_union_right _
        (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_range.2 (by omega))))) (hf (o n))

/-- The space as a topological space in `TopCat`. -/
abbrev Xsp : TopCat := TopCat.of Pt

theorem isOpenPt_of_opens (U : Opens Xsp) : IsOpenPt (U : Set Pt) := U.isOpen

theorem isOpenPt_basic (N : ℕ) : IsOpenPt (basic N) :=
  ⟨fun _ h => ⟨h, trivial⟩, fun _ h => h, fun _ => ⟨N, subset_rfl⟩⟩

/-- The basic neighbourhood `B_N` as an open set. -/
def basicOpen (N : ℕ) : Opens Xsp := ⟨basic N, isOpenPt_basic N⟩

/-- The basic neighbourhoods are a fundamental system of neighbourhoods of `infty`. -/
theorem exists_basicOpen_le {W : Opens Xsp} (hW : (infty : Xsp) ∈ W) :
    ∃ N, basicOpen N ≤ W :=
  (isOpenPt_of_opens W).2.2 hW

/-- The points of the `n`-th piece. -/
def InPiece (n : ℕ) : Pt → Prop
  | infty => False
  | c m => m = n
  | e m => m = n
  | o m => m = n
  | d m => m = n

/-- The `n`-th piece `{c n, e n, o n, d n}`, an open set. -/
def pieceOpen (n : ℕ) : Opens Xsp :=
  ⟨{y | InPiece n y}, ⟨fun _ h => ⟨h, h⟩, fun _ h => h, fun h => (h : False).elim⟩⟩

/-- The points `e n`, `o n`. -/
def InEO (n : ℕ) : Pt → Prop
  | infty => False
  | c _ => False
  | e m => m = n
  | o m => m = n
  | d _ => False

/-- The open set `{e n, o n}`. -/
def eoOpen (n : ℕ) : Opens Xsp :=
  ⟨{y | InEO n y}, ⟨fun _ h => (h : False).elim, fun _ h => h, fun h => (h : False).elim⟩⟩

theorem inEO_inBasic (N : ℕ) : ∀ y, InEO N y → InBasic N y
  | infty, h => (h : False).elim
  | c _, h => (h : False).elim
  | e m, h => by
    have : m = N := h
    show N ≤ m
    omega
  | o m, h => by
    have : m = N := h
    show N ≤ m
    omega
  | d _, h => (h : False).elim

theorem mem_o_of_c {U : Opens Xsp} {n : ℕ} (h : c n ∈ U) : o n ∈ U :=
  ((isOpenPt_of_opens U).1 n h).1

theorem mem_d_of_c {U : Opens Xsp} {n : ℕ} (h : c n ∈ U) : d n ∈ U :=
  ((isOpenPt_of_opens U).1 n h).2

theorem mem_o_of_e {U : Opens Xsp} {n : ℕ} (h : e n ∈ U) : o n ∈ U :=
  (isOpenPt_of_opens U).2.1 n h

/-! ### The structure sheaf -/

/-- The values of a section at each point: `k` at `infty` and `e n`, pairs `D × D` at the node
`c n` (its two branches), `K` at `o n` and `d n`. -/
@[reducible] def Val (k D K : Type) : Pt → Type
  | infty => k
  | c _ => D × D
  | e _ => k
  | o _ => K
  | d _ => K

instance instCommRingVal (k D K : Type) [CommRing k] [CommRing D] [CommRing K] :
    (y : Pt) → CommRing (Val k D K y)
  | infty => inferInstanceAs (CommRing k)
  | c _ => inferInstanceAs (CommRing (D × D))
  | e _ => inferInstanceAs (CommRing k)
  | o _ => inferInstanceAs (CommRing K)
  | d _ => inferInstanceAs (CommRing K)

/-- The sheaf of all functions with these values. -/
abbrev Fun (k D K : Type) : TopCat.Presheaf Type Xsp := TopCat.presheafToTypes Xsp (Val k D K)

/-- Sections of `Fun` over `U`. -/
abbrev Sec (k D K : Type) (U : Opens Xsp) : Type := (y : U) → Val k D K y.1

variable {k D K : Type} [CommRing k] [CommRing D] [CommRing K]

/-- The value at the node `c n`. -/
def atC {U : Opens Xsp} (s : Sec k D K U) {n : ℕ} (h : c n ∈ U) : D × D := s ⟨c n, h⟩

/-- The value at `e n`. -/
def atE {U : Opens Xsp} (s : Sec k D K U) {n : ℕ} (h : e n ∈ U) : k := s ⟨e n, h⟩

/-- The value at `o n`. -/
def atO {U : Opens Xsp} (s : Sec k D K U) {n : ℕ} (h : o n ∈ U) : K := s ⟨o n, h⟩

/-- The value at `d n`. -/
def atD {U : Opens Xsp} (s : Sec k D K U) {n : ℕ} (h : d n ∈ U) : K := s ⟨d n, h⟩

/-- The value at `infty`. -/
def atInf {U : Opens Xsp} (s : Sec k D K U) (h : (infty : Xsp) ∈ U) : k := s ⟨infty, h⟩

variable (κ : k →+* D) (ε : D →+* k) (ι : D →+* K)

/-- The constant sections near `infty`: the value `a ∈ k` read at each point. -/
def constHom : (y : Pt) → (k →+* Val k D K y)
  | infty => RingHom.id k
  | c _ => RingHom.prod κ κ
  | e _ => RingHom.id k
  | o _ => ι.comp κ
  | d _ => ι.comp κ

/-- At the node `c n`: the branches go to `o n` and `d n`, and have the same constant term. -/
def CondC (U : Opens Xsp) (s : Sec k D K U) : Prop :=
  ∀ n (h : c n ∈ U), ι (atC s h).1 = atO s (mem_o_of_c h) ∧ ι (atC s h).2 = atD s (mem_d_of_c h) ∧
    ε (atC s h).1 = ε (atC s h).2

/-- At `e n`: the constant goes to `o n`. -/
def CondE (U : Opens Xsp) (s : Sec k D K U) : Prop :=
  ∀ n (h : e n ∈ U), ι (κ (atE s h)) = atO s (mem_o_of_e h)

/-- At `infty`: near `infty`, the section is the constant given by its value at `infty`. -/
def CondInf (U : Opens Xsp) (s : Sec k D K U) : Prop :=
  ∀ h : (infty : Xsp) ∈ U, ∃ N, ∀ y : U, InBasic N y.1 → s y = constHom κ ι y.1 (atInf s h)

/-- **The structure sheaf `𝒪`.** -/
def O : Folder55.Subsheaf (Fun k D K) where
  sections U := {s | CondC ε ι U s ∧ CondE κ ι U s ∧ CondInf κ ι U s}
  restrict := by
    intro U V h s hs
    obtain ⟨hC, hE, hI⟩ := hs
    refine ⟨fun n hc => hC n (h hc), fun n he => hE n (h he), fun hi => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hI (h hi)
    exact ⟨N, fun y hy => hN ⟨y.1, h y.2⟩ hy⟩
  isLocal := by
    intro U s hs
    refine ⟨fun n hc => ?_, fun n he => ?_, fun hi => ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨V, _, hcV, hV⟩ := hs _ hc
      obtain ⟨hC, _, _⟩ := hV
      exact hC n hcV
    · obtain ⟨V, _, heV, hV⟩ := hs _ he
      obtain ⟨_, hE, _⟩ := hV
      exact hE n heV
    · obtain ⟨V, _, hiV, hV⟩ := hs _ hi
      obtain ⟨_, _, hI⟩ := hV
      obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := hI hiV
      obtain ⟨N', hN'⟩ := (isOpenPt_of_opens V).2.2 hiV
      refine ⟨max N N', fun y hy => ?_⟩
      have hyV : y.1 ∈ V := hN' (inBasic_anti (le_max_right _ _) _ hy)
      exact hN ⟨y.1, hyV⟩ (inBasic_anti (le_max_left _ _) _ hy)

theorem mem_O {U : Opens Xsp} {s : Sec k D K U} :
    s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U ↔ CondC ε ι U s ∧ CondE κ ι U s ∧ CondInf κ ι U s :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem O_one_mem (U : Opens Xsp) : (1 : Sec k D K U) ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U := by
  refine ⟨fun _ _ => ⟨?_, ?_, rfl⟩, fun _ _ => ?_, fun _ => ⟨0, fun y _ => ?_⟩⟩
  · show ι (1 : D) = (1 : K)
    exact map_one ι
  · show ι (1 : D) = (1 : K)
    exact map_one ι
  · show ι (κ (1 : k)) = (1 : K)
    rw [map_one, map_one]
  · show (1 : Val k D K y.1) = constHom κ ι y.1 (1 : k)
    exact (map_one (constHom κ ι y.1)).symm

theorem O_add_mem {U : Opens Xsp} {s t : Sec k D K U} (hs : s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U)
    (ht : t ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U) : s + t ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U := by
  obtain ⟨hsC, hsE, hsI⟩ := hs
  obtain ⟨htC, htE, htI⟩ := ht
  refine ⟨fun n h => ?_, fun n h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := hsC n h
    obtain ⟨h1', h2', h3'⟩ := htC n h
    refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · show ι (atC s h + atC t h).1 = atO s (mem_o_of_c h) + atO t (mem_o_of_c h)
      rw [Prod.fst_add, map_add, h1, h1']
    · show ι (atC s h + atC t h).2 = atD s (mem_d_of_c h) + atD t (mem_d_of_c h)
      rw [Prod.snd_add, map_add, h2, h2']
    · show ε (atC s h + atC t h).1 = ε (atC s h + atC t h).2
      rw [Prod.fst_add, Prod.snd_add, map_add, map_add, h3, h3']
  · show ι (κ (atE s h + atE t h)) = atO s (mem_o_of_e h) + atO t (mem_o_of_e h)
    rw [map_add, map_add, hsE n h, htE n h]
  · obtain ⟨N₁, hN₁⟩ := hsI h
    obtain ⟨N₂, hN₂⟩ := htI h
    refine ⟨max N₁ N₂, fun y hy => ?_⟩
    show s y + t y = constHom κ ι y.1 (atInf s h + atInf t h)
    rw [map_add, hN₁ y (inBasic_anti (le_max_left _ _) _ hy),
      hN₂ y (inBasic_anti (le_max_right _ _) _ hy)]

theorem O_mul_mem {U : Opens Xsp} {s t : Sec k D K U} (hs : s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U)
    (ht : t ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U) : s * t ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U := by
  obtain ⟨hsC, hsE, hsI⟩ := hs
  obtain ⟨htC, htE, htI⟩ := ht
  refine ⟨fun n h => ?_, fun n h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := hsC n h
    obtain ⟨h1', h2', h3'⟩ := htC n h
    refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · show ι (atC s h * atC t h).1 = atO s (mem_o_of_c h) * atO t (mem_o_of_c h)
      rw [Prod.fst_mul, map_mul, h1, h1']
    · show ι (atC s h * atC t h).2 = atD s (mem_d_of_c h) * atD t (mem_d_of_c h)
      rw [Prod.snd_mul, map_mul, h2, h2']
    · show ε (atC s h * atC t h).1 = ε (atC s h * atC t h).2
      rw [Prod.fst_mul, Prod.snd_mul, map_mul, map_mul, h3, h3']
  · show ι (κ (atE s h * atE t h)) = atO s (mem_o_of_e h) * atO t (mem_o_of_e h)
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, hsE n h, htE n h]
  · obtain ⟨N₁, hN₁⟩ := hsI h
    obtain ⟨N₂, hN₂⟩ := htI h
    refine ⟨max N₁ N₂, fun y hy => ?_⟩
    show s y * t y = constHom κ ι y.1 (atInf s h * atInf t h)
    rw [map_mul, hN₁ y (inBasic_anti (le_max_left _ _) _ hy),
      hN₂ y (inBasic_anti (le_max_right _ _) _ hy)]

/-! ### The Ideals `𝒢_j` -/

/-- **The Ideal `𝒢_j`**: sections of `𝒪` vanishing at `infty`, at every `d n`, and on the
pieces `n ≥ j`. -/
def G (j : ℕ) : Folder55.Subsheaf (Fun k D K) where
  sections U := {s | s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U ∧ ∀ y : U, InBasic j y.1 → (s : Sec k D K U) y = 0}
  restrict := by
    intro U V h s hs
    obtain ⟨hsO, hs0⟩ := hs
    exact ⟨(O κ ε ι).restrict h hsO, fun y hy => hs0 ⟨y.1, h y.2⟩ hy⟩
  isLocal := by
    intro U s hs
    refine ⟨(O κ ε ι).isLocal U s fun x hx => ?_, fun y hy => ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨V, hVU, hxV, hV⟩ := hs x hx
      obtain ⟨hVO, _⟩ := hV
      exact ⟨V, hVU, hxV, hVO⟩
    · obtain ⟨V, _, hyV, hV⟩ := hs y.1 y.2
      obtain ⟨_, hV0⟩ := hV
      exact hV0 ⟨y.1, hyV⟩ hy

theorem mem_G {j : ℕ} {U : Opens Xsp} {s : Sec k D K U} :
    s ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections U ↔
      s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U ∧ ∀ y : U, InBasic j y.1 → s y = 0 :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem G_le_O (j : ℕ) : G κ ε ι j ≤ O κ ε ι := by
  intro U s hs
  obtain ⟨h, _⟩ := hs
  exact h

theorem G_add_mem {j : ℕ} {U : Opens Xsp} {s t : Sec k D K U}
    (hs : s ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections U) (ht : t ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections U) :
    s + t ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections U := by
  obtain ⟨hsO, hs0⟩ := (mem_G κ ε ι).1 hs
  obtain ⟨htO, ht0⟩ := (mem_G κ ε ι).1 ht
  refine (mem_G κ ε ι).2 ⟨O_add_mem κ ε ι hsO htO, fun y hy => ?_⟩
  show s y + t y = 0
  rw [hs0 y hy, ht0 y hy, add_zero]

/-- `𝒢_j` is an Ideal: stable under multiplication by sections of `𝒪`. -/
theorem G_mul_mem {j : ℕ} {U : Opens Xsp} {s g : Sec k D K U}
    (hs : s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U) (hg : g ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections U) :
    s * g ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections U := by
  obtain ⟨hgO, hg0⟩ := (mem_G κ ε ι).1 hg
  refine (mem_G κ ε ι).2 ⟨O_mul_mem κ ε ι hs hgO, fun y hy => ?_⟩
  show s y * g y = 0
  rw [hg0 y hy, mul_zero]

theorem G_mono : Monotone (G κ ε ι) := by
  intro i j hij U s hs
  obtain ⟨hsO, hs0⟩ := hs
  exact ⟨hsO, fun y hy => hs0 y (inBasic_anti hij _ hy)⟩

/-! ### The identity principle at `infty` -/

/-- **Rigidity of a piece**: a section of `𝒪` defined on the piece `n` and vanishing at `d n`
vanishes at `c n`, `e n` and `o n`. -/
theorem rigid (hεκ : ∀ a, ε (κ a) = a) (hι : Function.Injective ι) {U : Opens Xsp}
    {s : Sec k D K U} (hs : s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections U) {n : ℕ} (hc : c n ∈ U) (he : e n ∈ U)
    (hd : atD s (mem_d_of_c hc) = 0) :
    atC s hc = 0 ∧ atE s he = 0 ∧ atO s (mem_o_of_c hc) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨hC, hE, _⟩ := (mem_O κ ε ι).1 hs
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := hC n hc
  have h4 := hE n he
  have hc2 : (atC s hc).2 = 0 := hι (by rw [h2, hd, map_zero])
  have hE' : κ (atE s he) = (atC s hc).1 := hι (h4.trans h1.symm)
  have hE0 : atE s he = 0 := by
    calc atE s he = ε (κ (atE s he)) := (hεκ _).symm
      _ = ε (atC s hc).1 := by rw [hE']
      _ = ε (atC s hc).2 := h3
      _ = 0 := by rw [hc2, map_zero]
  have hc1 : (atC s hc).1 = 0 := by rw [← hE', hE0, map_zero]
  refine ⟨Prod.ext hc1 hc2, hE0, ?_⟩
  rw [← h1, hc1, map_zero]

/-- **(v) for `𝒪` at `infty`, on every basic neighbourhood**: a section of `𝒪` over `B_M` which
vanishes on some open neighbourhood `W ⊆ B_M` of `infty` vanishes on `B_M`. -/
theorem identity_principle (hεκ : ∀ a, ε (κ a) = a) (hι : Function.Injective ι) (M : ℕ)
    {s : Sec k D K (basicOpen M)} (hs : s ∈ (O κ ε ι).sections (basicOpen M))
    {W : Opens Xsp} (hW : (infty : Xsp) ∈ W) (hWM : W ≤ basicOpen M)
    (h0 : ∀ y : W, s ⟨y.1, hWM y.2⟩ = 0) : s = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := (isOpenPt_of_opens W).2.2 hW
  have hdW : ∀ n, d n ∈ W := fun n => hN (show d n ∈ basic N from trivial)
  funext x
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := x
  cases y with
  | infty => exact h0 ⟨infty, hW⟩
  | d n => exact h0 ⟨d n, hdW n⟩
  | c n => exact (rigid κ ε ι hεκ hι hs hy (show e n ∈ basicOpen M from hy) (h0 ⟨d n, hdW n⟩)).1
  | e n =>
    exact (rigid κ ε ι hεκ hι hs (show c n ∈ basicOpen M from hy) hy (h0 ⟨d n, hdW n⟩)).2.1
  | o n =>
    exact (rigid κ ε ι hεκ hι hs (show c n ∈ basicOpen M from hy)
      (show e n ∈ basicOpen M from hy) (h0 ⟨d n, hdW n⟩)).2.2

/-- **No section of `𝒢_j` over a privileged neighbourhood**: `Γ(B_M, 𝒢_j) = 0`, although `𝒢_j`
is nonzero on `B_M` for `j > M`. -/
theorem G_sections_basic (hεκ : ∀ a, ε (κ a) = a) (hι : Function.Injective ι) (j M : ℕ)
    {s : Sec k D K (basicOpen M)} (hs : s ∈ (G κ ε ι j).sections (basicOpen M)) : s = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨hsO, hs0⟩ := (mem_G κ ε ι).1 hs
  exact identity_principle κ ε ι hεκ hι M hsO (W := basicOpen (max M j)) trivial
    (basic_anti (le_max_left M j)) fun y =>
      hs0 ⟨y.1, basic_anti (le_max_left M j) y.2⟩ (inBasic_anti (le_max_right M j) _ y.2)

/-! ### Germs stabilise, the sequence does not -/

/-- Subsheaves which agree on an open neighbourhood of `x` have the same germs at `x`. -/
theorem germs_eq_of_agreeOn {X : TopCat.{0}} {F : TopCat.Presheaf Type X}
    {S T : Folder55.Subsheaf F}
    {W : Opens X} {x : X} (hx : x ∈ W) (h : S.AgreeOn T W) : S.germs x = T.germs x := by
  have key : ∀ {S T : Folder55.Subsheaf F}, S.AgreeOn T W → S.germs x ⊆ T.germs x := by
    intro S T h
    rintro g ⟨U, hxU, s, hs, rfl⟩
    have hxUW : x ∈ U ⊓ W := ⟨hxU, hx⟩
    refine ⟨U ⊓ W, hxUW, F.map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s, ?_,
      F.germ_res_apply (homOfLE inf_le_left) x hxUW s⟩
    rw [← h (U ⊓ W) inf_le_right]
    exact S.restrict inf_le_left hs
  exact (key h).antisymm (key fun V hV => (h V hV).symm)

/-- At `infty` all the `𝒢_j` have the same germs (namely `0`). -/
theorem G_germs_inf (j : ℕ) : (G κ ε ι j).germs infty = (G κ ε ι 0).germs infty := by
  refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ (Folder55.Subsheaf.germs_mono (G_mono κ ε ι (Nat.zero_le j)) _)
  rintro g ⟨U, hx, s, hs, rfl⟩
  have hxW : (infty : Xsp) ∈ U ⊓ basicOpen j := ⟨hx, trivial⟩
  refine ⟨U ⊓ basicOpen j, hxW, (Fun k D K).map (homOfLE inf_le_left).op s, ?_,
    (Fun k D K).germ_res_apply (homOfLE inf_le_left) _ hxW s⟩
  obtain ⟨hsO, hs0⟩ := hs
  exact ⟨(O κ ε ι).restrict inf_le_left hsO, fun y _ => hs0 ⟨y.1, y.2.1⟩ y.2.2⟩

theorem inBasic_iff_of_inPiece {n j : ℕ} (hj : n + 1 ≤ j) :
    ∀ y, InPiece n y → (InBasic j y ↔ InBasic (n + 1) y)
  | infty, h => (h : False).elim
  | c m, h | e m, h | o m, h => by
    have : m = n := h
    show j ≤ m ↔ n + 1 ≤ m
    constructor <;> intro <;> omega
  | d _, _ => Iff.rfl

/-- On the piece `n`, the `𝒢_j` for `j ≥ n + 1` agree. -/
theorem G_agreeOn_piece {n j : ℕ} (hj : n + 1 ≤ j) :
    (G κ ε ι j).AgreeOn (G κ ε ι (n + 1)) (pieceOpen n) := by
  intro V hV
  ext s
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hsO, hs0⟩
    exact ⟨hsO, fun y hy => hs0 y ((inBasic_iff_of_inPiece hj y.1 (hV y.2)).2 hy)⟩
  · rintro ⟨hsO, hs0⟩
    exact ⟨hsO, fun y hy => hs0 y ((inBasic_iff_of_inPiece hj y.1 (hV y.2)).1 hy)⟩

/-- **The germs of the `𝒢_j` stabilise at every point.** -/
theorem G_germs_stabilize (x : Xsp) :
    ∃ j₀, ∀ j ≥ j₀, (G κ ε ι j).germs x = (G κ ε ι j₀).germs x := by
  cases x with
  | infty => exact ⟨0, fun j _ => G_germs_inf κ ε ι j⟩
  | c n => exact ⟨n + 1, fun j hj =>
      germs_eq_of_agreeOn (show c n ∈ pieceOpen n from (rfl : n = n)) (G_agreeOn_piece κ ε ι hj)⟩
  | e n => exact ⟨n + 1, fun j hj =>
      germs_eq_of_agreeOn (show e n ∈ pieceOpen n from (rfl : n = n)) (G_agreeOn_piece κ ε ι hj)⟩
  | o n => exact ⟨n + 1, fun j hj =>
      germs_eq_of_agreeOn (show o n ∈ pieceOpen n from (rfl : n = n)) (G_agreeOn_piece κ ε ι hj)⟩
  | d n => exact ⟨n + 1, fun j hj =>
      germs_eq_of_agreeOn (show d n ∈ pieceOpen n from (rfl : n = n)) (G_agreeOn_piece κ ε ι hj)⟩

/-- The section `1` over `{e j, o j}` lies in `𝒢_{j+1}`. -/
theorem one_mem_G_succ (j : ℕ) :
    (1 : Sec k D K (eoOpen j)) ∈ (G κ ε ι (j + 1)).sections (eoOpen j) := by
  refine ⟨⟨fun _ h => (h : False).elim, fun _ _ => ?_, fun h => (h : False).elim⟩, fun y hy => ?_⟩
  · show ι (κ (1 : k)) = (1 : K)
    rw [map_one, map_one]
  · exfalso
    obtain ⟨y, hyU⟩ := y
    cases y with
    | infty => exact (hyU : False).elim
    | c _ => exact (hyU : False).elim
    | e m =>
      have : j + 1 ≤ m := hy
      have : m = j := hyU
      omega
    | o m =>
      have : j + 1 ≤ m := hy
      have : m = j := hyU
      omega
    | d _ => exact (hyU : False).elim

/-- The section `1` over `{e j, o j}` does not lie in `𝒢_j`. -/
theorem one_not_mem_G [Nontrivial k] (j : ℕ) :
    (1 : Sec k D K (eoOpen j)) ∉ (G κ ε ι j).sections (eoOpen j) := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨_, h0⟩ := (mem_G κ ε ι).1 h
  have h1 := h0 ⟨e j, (rfl : j = j)⟩ (le_refl j)
  exact one_ne_zero (h1 : (1 : k) = 0)

/-- **The sequence `𝒢_j` is not stationary** — Lemme B fails for `F = 𝒪`. -/
theorem G_not_stationary [Nontrivial k] : ¬ ∃ j₀, ∀ j ≥ j₀, G κ ε ι j = G κ ε ι j₀ := by
  rintro ⟨j₀, hj₀⟩
  have hmem := one_mem_G_succ κ ε ι j₀
  rw [hj₀ (j₀ + 1) (Nat.le_succ j₀)] at hmem
  exact one_not_mem_G κ ε ι j₀ hmem

/-- **The uniformity hypothesis of `Folder55.stationary_of_germs` fails**: at `infty` the germs of
all the `𝒢_j` agree, but on no neighbourhood of `infty` do the `𝒢_j` agree with `𝒢_0`. -/
theorem G_not_uniform [Nontrivial k] :
    ¬ ∀ (x : Xsp) (j : ℕ), ∃ W : Opens Xsp, x ∈ W ∧
      ∀ l ≥ j, (G κ ε ι l).germs x = (G κ ε ι j).germs x → (G κ ε ι l).AgreeOn (G κ ε ι j) W := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hagree⟩ := h infty 0
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := (isOpenPt_of_opens W).2.2 hW
  have hle : eoOpen N ≤ W := fun y hy => hN (inEO_inBasic N y hy)
  have heq := hagree (N + 1) (Nat.zero_le _) (G_germs_inf κ ε ι (N + 1)) (eoOpen N) hle
  have hmem := one_mem_G_succ κ ε ι N
  rw [heq] at hmem
  exact one_not_mem_G κ ε ι N (G_mono κ ε ι (Nat.zero_le N) _ hmem)

/-- **Summary.** On the quasi-compact space `Xsp`, where the identity principle holds for `𝒪` at
`infty` on the fundamental system `B_M` (`identity_principle`), the increasing sequence of
Ideals `𝒢_j` has stabilising germs everywhere, fails the uniformity hypothesis of
`Folder55.stationary_of_germs`, and is not stationary. -/
theorem identity_principle_not_enough [Nontrivial k] :
    CompactSpace Xsp ∧ Monotone (G κ ε ι) ∧
      (∀ x : Xsp, ∃ j₀, ∀ j ≥ j₀, (G κ ε ι j).germs x = (G κ ε ι j₀).germs x) ∧
      (¬ ∀ (x : Xsp) (j : ℕ), ∃ W : Opens Xsp, x ∈ W ∧
        ∀ l ≥ j, (G κ ε ι l).germs x = (G κ ε ι j).germs x →
          (G κ ε ι l).AgreeOn (G κ ε ι j) W) ∧
      ¬ ∃ j₀, ∀ j ≥ j₀, G κ ε ι j = G κ ε ι j₀ :=
  ⟨inferInstanceAs (CompactSpace Pt), G_mono κ ε ι, G_germs_stabilize κ ε ι,
    G_not_uniform κ ε ι, G_not_stationary κ ε ι⟩

end Grothendieck.Folder55LemmaB
